.nh
.TH "GYRO" "1" "Nov 2026" "Gyro Hosting" "gyro manual"

.SH NAME
gyro-vpc-port-forward-update - Change a port forward (source allow list, name)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgyro vpc port-forward update   [--source  ... | --any] [--name ] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Only the given public IPv4 networks may use the forward (a single IP becomes /32; write the network
address, e.g. 198.51.100.0/24; at most 20). The list replaces the old one; --any opens it to everyone.
--name renames the forward (a label of at most 64 characters, "" removes it; the gateway is not touched).
What you leave out does not change.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--any\fP[=false]
	allow everyone (empty list)

.PP
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	show the request without changing anything

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for update

.PP
\fB--name\fP=""
	new name (label, at most 64 characters; "" removes it)

.PP
\fB--source\fP=[]
	allowed source IPv4 or CIDR (repeatable or comma separated)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--api-url\fP=""
	API base URL (env GYRO_API_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	log HTTP requests to stderr (secrets masked)

.PP
\fB--lang\fP=""
	message language: tr or en (default from locale)

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	disable colours (also NO_COLOR)

.PP
\fB--no-header\fP[=false]
	omit the table header

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=""
	output format: table, json, yaml, text

.PP
\fB-p\fP, \fB--profile\fP=""
	profile to use (env GYRO_PROFILE)

.PP
\fB--query\fP=""
	JMESPath query applied to the result

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	print only ids

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=0s
	overall timeout, e.g. 30s, 10m

.PP
\fB--wide\fP[=false]
	show all table columns

.PP
\fB-y\fP, \fB--yes\fP[=false]
	do not ask for confirmation


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  gyro vpc port-forward update vpc-1a2b3c4d pf-9c8b7a6d --source 203.0.113.10 --source 198.51.100.0/24
  gyro vpc port-forward update vpc-1a2b3c4d pf-9c8b7a6d --any
  gyro vpc port-forward update vpc-1a2b3c4d pf-9c8b7a6d --name ssh-admin
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgyro-vpc-port-forward(1)\fP
